'''Synthesised items''' have their base [[implicit]] modifiers replaced with up to three [[List of synthesised implicit modifiers|Synthesis implicit modifiers]]. These are potentially very powerful modifiers that can't be obtained otherwise.

Currently, synthesised items can only be found as unique item drops from [[List of unique synthesis maps|Synthesis]] bosses. The only way to obtain a non-unique synthesised item outside of Standard leagues is to [[Corrupted|corrupt]] a unique synthesised item into a non-unique item.

__TOC__

== Mechanics ==
[[File:Synthesised item.png|thumb|A {{il|Highborn Bow}} with one Synthesised implicit modifier]]
* Synthesised items are items with one to three [[Synthesised implicit modifier]]s. Except the implicit, a synthesised item has the same [[defences]], {{Tooltip|APS|Attacks per Second}} or damage values as the normal base, as well as [[attribute]] requirements. They also have "Synthesised" as a prefix of their name, as well as [[File:Synthesised-item-symbol.png]] symbol in front and at the back of their name.
* Corrupted implicits may replace Synthesised implicits through [[Corrupted|corruption]]. Each corrupted implicit replaces one Synthesised implicit; items can have a mix of both. 
* Like other modifiers, it is possible for a Synthesised implicit modifier to change an item's required level if the 80% of the implicit's item level requirement is higher than the item's default required level (e.g. a synthesised implicit modifier requiring Level 56 to roll will add a required Level of 44). Conversely, for most [[jewellery]] or [[quiver]]s, if a Synthesised implicit's required level is lower than the item's default level, it can lower the default required level of the item (though it will still be restricted by the required level of explicit modifiers).
* Synthesised items can be [[enchantment|enchanted]], which doesn't affect implicits.
* A [[normal]] Synthesised item cannot be turned into a [[unique item]] using an {{il|Orb of Chance}}. 
* Synthesised items cannot be [[Fractured item|fractured]] or given an [[Influenced item|influenced modifiers]].
* Synthesised items ''can'' gain [[eldritch implicit modifier]]s, but all existing Synthesised implicits will be removed; it is not possible to have a mix of eldritch and Synthesised implicits. The item base will still be Synthesised (e.g. still cannot be fractured).
* Synthesised items used in a [[Vendor recipe system|vendor recipe]] which modifies the item, e.g. by adding a fixed modifier, will have the Synthesised implicit mod removed.
* Synthesised items can have [[Imprint]]s applied to them. It is even possible to roll back Synthesising the item, if the imprint was created before the Harvest Synthesis craft was performed.

[[Beastcrafting]] with a [[Vivid Vulture]] allows the rerolling of Synthesis implicit modifiers on unique items.

==Synthesised implicit modifiers==
{{See also|List of synthesised implicit modifiers|List of corrupted synthesis modifiers}}

Synthesised implicit modifiers replace any implicit modifiers that items have normally.

